  "kill_criteria": [
    "Kill a tapeout if a quality- and SLO-matched commodity implementation does not first deliver at least 1.5x lower measured cost per token on two models.",
    "Kill the hardware thesis if the residual gain attributable to custom silicon is below 30 percent after commodity Rubin or MI450, persistent-kernel, and model-change baselines.",
    "Kill the current profile if measured end-to-end expert dispatch cannot sustain 60 percent of its declared fabric bandwidth or its p99 coordination term exceeds the modeled value by 2x.",
    "Kill a single-package plan if capacity needs more HBM stacks than a qualified package supports with supplier-backed usable capacity, power, thermal, and yield margins.",
    "Kill the current package if landed accelerator power exceeds 1.5 kW without a funded liquid-cooling deployment path, or if the serving rack exceeds 150 kW without facility and utilization economics.",
    "Kill the program if a foundry, HBM, packaging, and test quote plus risk-adjusted respin reserve cannot be repaid within three years by contracted token volume under incumbent price decline.",
    "Kill any 5x claim until the full active GLM ledger, contention, queueing, quality, measured timing, energy, and fully loaded dollars are all present."
  ],
